    <task id="LOCAL-00030" summary="Remove the error-code (if any) from stack in interrupt/exception handler upfront before saving the registers to ensure rsp is 16 byte aligned. without error-code, the stack has 5 params * 8 byte = 40 bytes. Save registers will push 120 bytes for registers and 512 bytes for xxm registers - total 512 + 120 + 40 = 672 -&gt; 16 byte aligned. Adding error-code will make rsp 680 bytes which is not 16 byte aligned, which makes fxsave fail with General Protection Fault">
      <created>1709547510224</created>
      <option name="number" value="00030" />
      <option name="presentableId" value="LOCAL-00030" />
      <option name="project" value="LOCAL" />
      <updated>1709547510224</updated>
    </task>
    <task id="LOCAL-00031" summary="separate stack frame for timer vs page-fault vs rest. It is paricurlarly important to keep stack separate for time vs page-fault because page-fault handler yields by calling timer interrupt (int 0x20) and hence they can't both use same stack frame. This is achieved using different IST values in IDT definition of these interrupts">
      <created>1709547758990</created>
